    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.67), our two most potent assets. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a substantial +16% park adjustment and a prime leadoff spot, making him our premier play despite a modest SP skill drag against Warren. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.08) also provide elite stability, both buoyed by favorable platoon dynamics that elevate their projected output well above their baseline stats. We are particularly leveraging the favorable matchups against Singer and Houser, as the offensive core displays a strong collective floor across the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (56.92), who fell just shy of the threshold. While **Josh Jung** possesses the raw talent to outperform the back-end starters, the optimizer favored the higher dynamic platoon advantages held by the likes of **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez** in the **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** stack. We continue to monitor the SB-heavy profile of **Josh Lowe** (63.35); despite a negative adjustment for an elite catcher, his high-efficiency base makes him a must-start in our pursuit of category scarcity. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Liam Hicks** and **Sam Antonacci**, as both hover near the 59-point mark; they remain in the lineup based on volume, but we are ready to pivot if early weather reports or late lineup shifts materialize.",
